### ba17138438 fix(sync): validate rival before delete; weight-first fork choice

Two correctness fixes to `8b82864c9` found in review:

- **Validate before delete (push path).** `_resolve_fork` deleted our
  blocks and committed before `_append_block` validated the rival — a
  malformed or malicious block claiming a winning `(round, hash)` could
  knock the head off any validator whose losing segment was empty (most
  heads, since heartbeat blocks are empty), repeatable as a grief loop.
  The rival now passes signature, timestamp sanity (≥ parent ts, within
  one proposer window of future skew), and the proposer schedule for the
  round its timestamp claims BEFORE any delete is staged, and the
  delete+append share one transaction — `_append_block`'s failure paths
  roll back our row. `_resolve_fork_with_peer` got the same ordering:
  every fetched peer-segment block is validated (signature, timestamp,
  schedule) before our losing segment is removed.
- **Branch weight decides, not the fork-point key.** `(round, hash)`
  alone let an isolated node win: a lone validator owns the first
  contested round ~1/4 of the time, so its fork-point block outranked the
  majority's deeper-but-later-round segment. The pull resolver now
  compares, in order, distinct proposers in each segment (a lone node's
  branch shows 1; the majority's up to N−1), then segment length, then
  `(round, hash)` — every quantity derivable from headers, still fully
  deterministic, but the round only settles ties between equally
  supported branches. The push path reorgs only a pure tip race (rival
  shares our head's parent AND our head has no descendants); deeper
  conflicts defer to the pull resolver.

New metric `sync_fork_invalid_rival_total`. 17 fork-choice tests +
224-test sync/consensus suite pass; ruff/mypy clean.

- **RPC block-header cache expiry (commit 591bb295b0).** The live fork
  test exposed a follow-up defect: after the pull resolver reorged height
  25841 to the majority block, /rpc/block/25841 kept serving the
  orphaned header. aitbc-blockchain-rpc is a separate process from the
  node that performs imports/reorgs, so in-process invalidate() calls
  never reached its cache, and the cache assumed height→hash was
  immutable (true before reorgs existed). BlockHeaderCache entries now
  expire ttl_seconds after insertion (default 120s, ~2 block
  intervals; <=0 keeps the old unbounded behaviour). Verified live: all
  five nodes' /rpc/block/25841 now return the canonical 0x5074c6f6…
  majority block. 20 cache tests pass including new TTL/reorg-replacement
  coverage.

### edge reverse-proxy normalization + verification (2026-09-27)

Fleet nginx edge audit found four live defects; all fixed and verified:

- **node0 had no `real_ip` config** — external clients appeared as the edge
  IP `10.1.223.1`, breaking per-IP rate limits and client logging. Added
  `set_real_ip_from` + `real_ip_header X-Forwarded-For` (non-recursive: the
  last XFF element is edge-appended and trustworthy; recursion would honour
  client-injected entries). Verified: request from hub logs `152.53.242.245`.
- **WS idle teardown asymmetry** — hub1's edge granted 3600s on
  `/rpc/{subscribe,gossip}/ws` + `/agent/`; hub's edge (ns2) and the IDE
  edges (node0/1/2) fell back to the 60s default, silently tearing idle
  gossip/subscribe/agent-SSE streams. Matching 3600s blocks deployed to
  ns2 and all three IDE confs.
- **hub1 edge catch-all could not WS-upgrade** — missing
  `proxy_http_version 1.1` + Upgrade headers degraded non-whitelisted WS
  paths to HTTP/1.0. Fixed.
- **Cleanups:** stale `set_real_ip_from 10.1.223.1` + orphaned
  `real_ip_recursive` removed from hub's nginx.conf (leftover from hub's
  pre-netcup placement); node1's `aitbc_backend` upstream dropped its
  duplicate member (LAN IP == same process as loopback); `/etc/nginx`
  backup litter on hub/hub1/node2 archived to
  `/root/nginx-conf-archive-20260927/` per host.

Verified live: `/health` 200 on all five public names; `/rpc/subscribe/ws`
handshake → 101 fleet-wide, `/rpc/gossip/ws` → 403 (app-level peer auth);
fully idle WS through hub's edge survived 80s (pre-fix teardown at 60s);
gossip conn snapshot stable (32/22/26/30/30). Full topology written to
TOPOLOGY.md (operator notes).

