## 2026-09-28 — fork-recovery drills: delta-journal undo verified against real data (fix in this batch)

The non-empty-undo path (SYNC_FORK_UNDO_ENABLED, default on) had never
executed against real production data — only unit and differential tests.
Two drills closed that gap:

**Drill A (copy of node2 chain.db):** reverted a 146-block real segment
(26724..26869, all journal_status=complete) — ancestor state root and the
gpu_registration side-table digest both verified, all block/tx/journal
rows removed. All 5 orphaned txs re-admitted through full admission into
the mempool (signed envelopes, nonces/balances valid post-revert).
Fabricated lost-tx lifecycle verified end-to-end: unsigned orphan ->
admission reject -> sync_fork_orphaned_tx_lost_total +1 ->
sync_fork_domain_rows_orphaned_total +1 -> stake row orphaned -> insert
confirmed lock -> _revive_confirmed_domain_rows restored it to active.

**Drill B (live node0):** sent canary TRANSFER 0xcf2282 (confirmed
26881), stopped the node, reverted [26881..26882] on the live chain.db
via revert_losing_segment (ancestor root verified), requeued the orphan
through real admission, restarted. node0 bulk-pulled the identical
winning branch (0xefca65aacc0feebd), canary re-confirmed at 26881,
fleet reconverged hash-identical at 26886 with zero fork/divergence
errors. Post-import reconcile classified the orphan on-chain -> not
lost.

Findings along the way:

- MEMPOOL_BACKEND drift: node0 alone runs 'memory' (fleet default
  'database'). Harmless today — node0 never proposes, so nothing drains
  either backend — but requeue/evict on node0 operate on an in-memory
  pool while its postgres aitbc_mempool table is written only by the
  rpc service. Flagged for the operator; left as found.
- CLI canary note: 'aitbc transactions send --type GPU_REGISTER' fails
  apply with 'must have value=0' since the CLI requires --amount>0;
  the earlier gpu canary used the raw signed-RPC path.
- bridge_block_header digest-cap concern resolved: written only by the
  bridge finalizer (own session), can never enter a block journal, so
  the 100k digest cap is unreachable for it. Code comment added at
  _DIGEST_EXCLUDE; behavior kept fail-closed if ever journaled.
- Pre-existing stale mempool row 0xde13acc on node0's postgres mempool
  (legacy format, no tx_hash in content) — predates the drill, left as
  found.

## 2026-09-28 — .devin/ untracked (repo hygiene)

`.devin/` carried operator-side Devin agent config: `mcp_config.json`
hardcoding `/opt/aitbc` + `/usr/local/bin/aitbc` paths, an MCP permission
policy, and a private-Gitea `tea` skill — all meaningless or misleading for
public cloners (and dead weight on node checkouts, where no Devin sessions
run). Untracked the whole tree; `.gitignore` now covers `.devin/`
superseding the narrower `*.local.json` rule. Local copies stay in the IDE
checkout; the tea skill moved to `~/.config/devin/skills/` for global use.
